Two grid polish items, same discipline as IL-0070 (lock_draft → Vibe Check → wait for my yes → run_locked only → report; no commits, no co-author trailers). Tree is at 7b81455, your grid commit — clean apart from the usual unstaged files.
1. Double-click landing — real bug, mechanism already located. In grid, double-click a sheet: it opens in Single pinned to the LEFT edge of the canvas whenever the canvas is wider than the window (zoom in a little to reproduce). ScriptSurface.showPage scrolls the clip to NSPoint(x: 0, y: …) — document origin, not the picked page. It should centre the picked page horizontally: x = frame.midX - clip.bounds.width / 2, clamped to the document. Also check the ordering: setArrangement(.single) fires scrollBack(to: anchor) with an anchor measured in grid coordinates before showPage scrolls again — two competing scrolls; make the final resting position deterministic: picked page centred horizontally, its top near the viewport top as now, caret on its first line. Pin it with a test: canvas wider than the clip, showPage(3), assert the page's frame is horizontally centred in the visible rect.
2. Marker and number scale at grid size — taste fix, measured. NoteMarker.size is 16pt, designed for a life-size sheet; at grid scale (~0.4×) the bubbles dominate the card. Scale the drawn marker with the card scale (floor around 10–11pt) while keeping a 16pt hit area so they stay clickable — hit-test padding, not a bigger draw. Drop the foot number a step with them (it should read as a caption, not a headline). Single and Two-page marker sizes must not change. Extend GridMapTests: marker draw size shrinks in grid and does not in single; the contrast test keeps passing.
Budget: PageCanvasView.swift, ScriptSurface.swift, NoteMarker.swift (only if the hit-area needs it), GridMapTests.swift, DiscreteSheetsTests.swift only if an existing test encodes the old landing. Deny: everything else, as before. Proof: surface suite green (302, 6 skipped), macOS Debug build with your private DerivedData, and report both before/after behavior in the Change Report. No commit.